    51	<tr><td>"Current estimates situate the production of the microfusion cell in the 1990s, or even later" (p. 28)</td><td>Not arrived, and not scoreable against him: he is repeating a contemporary consensus, not forecasting, and "or even later" sets no bound. The programme is live and expensive <!-- CHECK: fusion-spending --></td><td class="verdict v-open">OPEN</td></tr>
    52	<tr><td>Radioactive waste is a problem "we still do not know what we should do about" (p. 29), offered as the surprise bill a cure brings</td><td>Still true sixty years later: as of August 2026 no spent fuel has been permanently disposed of, the first deep repository still awaiting its licence <!-- CHECK: onkalo-2026 --></td><td class="verdict v-hit">HIT</td></tr>
    53	<tr><td colspan="3"><strong>Problem level</strong></td></tr>
    54	<tr><td>The straight line: "we are always inclined to extend the course of new technologies into the future by means of straight lines" (p. 28)</td><td>Confirmed on his own work by this book's strictest verdict: the air-cushion successor was the impressive machine of its moment extended forward, and the wheels stayed <!-- CHECK: hovercraft-2000 --> <!-- CHECK: ev-share-2025 --></td><td class="verdict v-hit">HIT</td></tr>
